{# Widget "kinds" — what these files are (FL·07).

   STATIC TWIN of files.widgets.js's `kinds` entry. Rendered by BOTH the hub and
   the widget library.

   One hue at varying strength: a quantity is one quantity, and three colours for
   three shares of the same total would be three claims about unrelated things. #}
{% set bars = ['', 'b', 'c'] %}
<div class="c" data-w="kinds">
    <span class="tab">What these files are</span>
    <div class="f-use">
        {% for row in byKind %}
            <div class="f-userow">
                <div class="top"><b>{{ row.kind.plural }}</b><span class="sub">{{ row.bytes|storage_bytes }}</span><span class="n">{{ row.files|number_format(0, '.', ' ') }}</span></div>
                <div class="f-bar"><i class="{{ bars[loop.index0] ?? 'c' }}" style="width:{{ row.share }}%"></i></div>
            </div>
        {% else %}
            <div class="use" style="margin-bottom:0">No files yet, so nothing to divide up.</div>
        {% endfor %}
    </div>
    <div class="use"><b>Only photographs get a small picture.</b> A PDF and a GPX have nothing to shrink, so their tiles say what they are instead of pretending to be broken images. The allowlist is on the <b>detected</b> type, never on the file&rsquo;s name &mdash; renaming a thing does not change what it is.</div>
</div>
